{"id": 29, "ts": 1783929244.7877324, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I appreciate the strong cases made for both Candidate\u202fA and Candidate\u202fC. However, the missing evidence on A\u2019s technical competence\u2014particularly weather assessment and navigation\u2014leaves a critical gap for a long\u2011distance pilot. Candidate\u202fC, while technically outstanding, raises serious crew\u2011cooperation concerns (unfriendly, not open to new ideas) that could jeopardize cockpit harmony on long hauls.\nCandidate\u202fB, on the other hand, offers a balanced profile: he is very conscientious (high operational reliability), handles stress well, and demonstrably possesses technical skills relevant to long\u2011distance operations (good at assessing weather conditions and excellent computer skills). Although he is sometimes perceived as pretentious and may adopt the wrong tone, these communication issues appear less severe than A\u2019s egocentric attitude and C\u2019s unfriendly demeanor, and can be mitigated through crew\u2011resource\u2011management training.\nGiven the need for solid technical competence combined with reliable, calm performance, I would shift my provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fB**. This choice addresses the most safety\u2011critical criteria while keeping crew\u2011cooperation concerns manageable."}
